  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Delivering lifesaving sexual and reproductive health services, gender&#x2013;based violence response and mental health and psychosocial support in North-West Myanmar (Chin, Rakhine and Sagaing)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide gender-based violence (GBV) and health assistance to vulnerable communities affected by conflict in Myanmar. This UNFPA project provides access to sexual and reproductive health services, supplies clean delivery and dignity kits, and provides case management as well as psychosocial support to victims of GBV, among other activities. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 2,700 people in the Health sector and 15,000 people in the Protection &#x2013; GBV sector.</narrative>
  </description>
